  "notes": "Inventory is the complete developer-facing surface shipped in the Chrome 153 dev trial: one Document attribute plus the interface's two methods (the SpellCheckCustomDictionary interface has no other members; the exemption-list concept, matching semantics, and Chrome's 20,000-word/128-byte limits are documented in the overview's #matching-and-limits section referenced from all three items' documentation). The draft WHATWG PR names the attribute spellCheckDictionary with [Exposed=Document] and no SecureContext, while the shipped surface is spellCheckCustomDictionary with [Exposed=Window, SecureContext] [SameObject]; the overview's Syntax section transcribes both IDLs verbatim and enumerates the discrepancies rather than presenting either alone as settled. Limits (20,000 words / 128 UTF-8 bytes) are Chrome implementation values from the owners' Dev Trial instructions, labelled as such; the explainer leaves limits implementation-defined."
